.TH SANCHALA-ACCESSIBILITY 1 "August 2026" "Sanchala OS" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sanchala-accessibility \- Accessibility tools for Sanchala OS
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sanchala-accessibility
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fICOMMAND\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sanchala-accessibility
manages accessibility features including screen reader, magnification,
high contrast modes, and keyboard navigation.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B status
Show accessibility status
.TP
.B reader \fR[\fBon\fR|\fBoff\fR]
Toggle screen reader (Orca)
.TP
.B magnifier \fR[\fBon\fR|\fBoff\fR|\fILEVEL\fR]
Toggle/set magnification
.TP
.B contrast \fR[\fBnormal\fR|\fBhigh\fR|\fBinvert\fR]
Set contrast mode
.TP
.B keyboard
Configure keyboard accessibility
.TP
.B cursor
Configure cursor size and visibility
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-json
Output in JSON format
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show help message
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/sanchala/accessibility/
System configuration
.TP
.I ~/.config/sanchala/accessibility.toml
User preferences
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR orca (1),
.BR sanchala-voice (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Sanchala OS Team <dev@sanchala.id>
